\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Saviour from sin, I wait to prove 
\par That Jesus is Thy healing name;
\par The lose, when perfected in love,
\par Whate'er I have, or can, or am
\par I stay me on Thy faithful word:
\par The servant shall be as his Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Answer that gracious end in me
\par For which Thy precious life was given;
\par Redeem from all iniquity;
\par Restore, and make me meet for heaven:
\par Unless Thou purge my every stain,
\par Thy suffering and my faith are vain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Didst Thou not die that I might live
\par No longer to myself, but Thee,
\par Might body, soul, and spirit give 
\par To Him who gave Himself for me?
\par Come then, my Master, and my God,
\par Take the dear purchase of Thy blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy own perculiar servant claim,
\par For Thy own truth and mercy's sake;
\par Hallow in me Thy glorious name;
\par Me for Thine own this moment take,
\par And change, and throughly purify;
\par Thine only may I live and die.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

